      "op": "entity.declare",
      "local_ref": "claim",
      "kind": "claim",
      "title": "Monoidal relaxation derives additive N and Z but not Carrier multiplication",
      "status": "conditional_on_explicit_monoidal_relaxation",
      "demonstrated_strength": [
        "unbounded additive universal-property theorem",
        "exact finite normalization control"
      ],
      "body": "Conditionally replace the unproved categorical coproduct by the established symmetric-monoidal geometric disjoint union and fix a connected source-derived surface U. The mapping-class subgroupoid generated by U and the empty surface has unique connected-component normal forms; its pi_0 is therefore the free commutative monoid on U, identified with N by universal property rather than by an input cardinality label. Pair completion modulo simultaneous stabilization is the free abelian group on U, hence Z. This conditional additive derivation does not provide a semiring: existence of a second distributive tensor with unit U remains unproved, and the exact unmarked quadrilateral sewing candidate has fixed-point deficit 1. The finalized literal coproduct gate remains failed and the relaxation is not adopted.",
      "entity_id": "claim:024f2ece848b6c857fe7"
    },
