      "intent": "result",
      "sent_at": "2026-08-20T18:39:57.011Z",
      "body": "Under an explicit symmetric-monoidal relaxation, finite disjoint unions of one connected U form the free commutative monoid and their intrinsic pair completion is the free abelian group, yielding additive N and Z by universal properties. This does not yet support Burnside-Witt: no second distributive Carrier tensor with unit U is derived, and the smallest unmarked connected sewing has fixed-point deficit 1. The relaxation is analyzed rather than adopted. Packet: research/grothendieck/phase-i-monoidal-additive-completion.md.",
